\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. With the sweet word of peace
\par We bid our brethren go;
\par Peace, as a river, to increase
\par And ceaseless flow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. With the calm word of prayer
\par We earnestly commend
\par Our brethren to Thy watchful care,
\par Eternal Friend!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. With the dear word of love
\par We give our brief farewell;
\par Our love below, and Thine above,
\par With them shall dwell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With the strong word of faith,
\par We stay ourselves on Thee;
\par That Thou, O Lord, in life and death
\par Their help shall be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then the bright word of hope
\par Shall on our parting gleam,
\par And tell of joys beyond the scope
\par Of earth- born dream.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Farewell; in hope, and love,
\par In faith, and peace, and prayer,
\par Till He whose home is ours above
\par Unite us there.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

